A||||4||billfredmike24||How to get the power windows down??||||1||
Z||000000||billfredmike24||08-06-2001||01:15 AM||||I'm trying to remove the power mirrors and the door skins from an 85 gt, i have no power source and was wondering if there's a way to get the power windows down without having a battery installed.  It's a parts car and has no engine, just loose wires , and the positive battery wire has been cut?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_10.jpg"> <BR>yeah the wheels are ugly, and the stickers, that'll change||||reg||1
Z||000001||BC-GT||08-06-2001||01:44 AM||||Don't have an answer to your question, but was wondering if you are selling the wing, being a parts car and all.<P>------------------<BR>Darryl Martin<BR>1985 GT <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.imagestation.com/picture/pf251a969c96964ef15691e97e7ac4489/feb64e3a.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||cadaver||08-06-2001||01:50 AM||||Just hook a battery straight to the leads and run it down.||||reg||1
Z||000003||billfredmike24||08-06-2001||01:50 PM||||BC the one in the pic is not the parts car, there's no wing on the parts car.<BR>cadaver, can you tell me exactly how to do this.<BR>Thanks MIke||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierohoho||08-06-2001||07:16 PM||||I just picked up two doors at the junk yard with power windows and had to run them down so the glass doesn't break while I store them ,here's what I did.<P>The rubber boot that goes from the door to the frame can be pulled away from the frame which will expose the plug.<P>Un-plug the connection.<P>The plug that goes into the door will have two heavier wires a dark blue and a tan/brown These are the ones you use.<P>There are others but they don't connect to the window motor and are smaller in diameter than the two you use.<P>The following can be done with a battery charger or a good 12v battery, I used a charger.<P>I put the Negative(-) terminal from my battery charger on the door itself (On a metal spot for good ground).<P>I put a small screwdriver into the positive(+) battery charger clip.<P><BR>I used a small nail and touched it to the blue wire and the other end of the nail was touching the door(again a good metal ground) and I put the positive(+) to the brown and the window rolled down.<P>Now I'm not positive if I had the blue as a ground or the brown but once you get set up it's not too hard to try it both ways.<P>I hope thats not too confusing and will help, if you need clarification post back. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l||||reg||1
